{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785341852,"nonce":"GCzM0TUBMOvu4f3LKw+YUmgmjH0=","message":"Implemented on master as commit a8f5392: 'b4 review cron' runs the full maintenance sweep (wake snoozes, rescan branches, update all series, deliver the thanks queue) non-interactively. --update / --deliver-queue select task groups, --dry-run reports what queue delivery would do, --sign opts into patatt signing (off by default for timer processes). Bare cron works on the enrolled repo containing the cwd, or on all known projects when run from elsewhere (schedulers); -i is repeatable to pick specific projects. Queue delivery and the update sweep hold flocks shared with the TUI, so cron and an interactive session can never double-send. Docs include a systemd user service/timer example and a post-push wrapper.","files":null}]}